# PLP Design System Alignment Sprint
## Post-Homepage Products Discovery UI — Audit Remediation

> **Source Audit**: `01_audit_ratings_and_gaps.md`
> **End-State Spec**: `03_end_state_specifications.md`
> **Goal**: Close all 20 audit gaps (G-01 through G-20) to achieve professional PLP that implements the design system fully and maintains homepage editorial-luxury personality.

---

## Scope Lock Rules

- **NO** changes to `globals.css` — scoped Tailwind only
- **NO** homepage content/layout changes — regression containment required
- **NO** data structure changes — VFS and Sanity schemas frozen
- **NO** arbitrary values — design system tokens only
- **NO** new npm dependencies

---

## Pre-Sprint Regression Containment

### At-Risk Code Areas Identified

| Area | File(s) | Risk | Containment Strategy |
|------|---------|------|---------------------|
| Homepage Cards | `AccessoryCard.tsx`, `DacCard.tsx`, `IemCard.tsx`, `Featured/card/Card.tsx` | Use `.card-product` class or `shadow-card` tokens | Visual regression tests for homepage product cards |
| Tailwind Config | `tailwind.config.ts` — `.card-product` component class | Changing shadow tokens affects light-surface cards | Create `.card-product-dark` variant instead of modifying base class |
| Other Product Grids | Check all `ProductGrid` imports | Layout changes may affect other pages | Component-level isolation, page-specific wrappers |

### Regression Tests (Run Before & After Sprint)

```bash
# 1. Homepage Product Cards Visual Check
npm run build
npx playwright test --grep "homepage" --reporter=list

# 2. PLP Page Renders Without Error
curl -s http://localhost:3000/products/headphones/open-back | head -20

# 3. Build Passes
npm run build

# 4. No Tailwind Class Errors
grep -r "shadow-card" app/ --include="*.tsx" | wc -l  # Should remain 6 (current count)
```

---

## Sprint Architecture

### Pass Sequencing

**Pass 1 — Skeleton Pass (all components, no styling)**
- All 10 scope contracts: semantic HTML/JSX structure only
- No Tailwind classes beyond layout primitives
- No colors, no typography, no borders

**Pass 2 — Data Pass (all components, real data, no styling)**
- All 10 scope contracts: integrate real data flow
- Props drilling verified
- No visual styling yet

**Pass 3 — Build Pass (one component at a time, full scope)**
- Desktop-first (1280px), then mobile (375px)
- Layer 1→2→3→4 per component

### Layer Sequencing (Per Component in Pass 3)

```
Layer 1 — Structure:    Semantic HTML/JSX skeleton. No classes. No logic.
Layer 2 — Layout:       Tailwind flex/grid/spacing/sizing only.
                        No colors. No typography. No borders.
Layer 3 — Surface:      Colors, typography, brand tokens, imagery.
Layer 4 — Interaction:  Hover states, transitions, animations.
```

---

## Scope Contracts (10 Total)

---

### Scope Contract 1: Global Design System — Shadow Tokens
**Gap Coverage**: G-14 (Shadows — Dark-Surface)

**Current State**: `.card-product` uses `boxShadow.card` designed for light surfaces. On dark PLP background, shadows are invisible.

**Target State**:
- Add `.card-product-dark` component class using `cardDark`/`cardDarkHover` tokens
- Leave `.card-product` untouched (homepage regression containment)
- PLP cards use `.card-product-dark`

**DoD — Pass 1: Skeleton**
- [ ] Audit all files using `.card-product` (6 files identified)
- [ ] Document which files should use `.card-product` vs `.card-product-dark`
- [ ] Add `.card-product-dark` class definition in `tailwind.config.ts` (structure only, no styling)

**DoD — Pass 2: Data**
- [ ] Verify `cardDark`/`cardDarkHover` tokens exist in tailwind config
- [ ] Confirm token values match spec: `0 0 0 1px rgba(246,227,213,0.06), 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)`

**DoD — Pass 3: Build (Desktop → Mobile)**

*Layer 1 — Structure*
- [ ] Add `.card-product-dark` CSS component class in `tailwind.config.ts`

*Layer 2 — Layout*
- [ ] Same padding/spacing as `.card-product`
- [ ] Border and radius structure in place

*Layer 3 — Surface*
- [ ] Apply `boxShadow.cardDark` token
- [ ] Border color: `border.secondary`
- [ ] Background: transparent

*Layer 4 — Interaction*
- [ ] Hover: `boxShadow.cardDarkHover`
- [ ] Hover: `border-brand-400`
- [ ] Hover: `translateY(-2px)`
- [ ] Transition: `all 300ms ease-out`

**Verification**
```bash
# Verify tokens exist
grep -A2 "cardDark:" tailwind.config.ts
# Verify class added
grep "card-product-dark" tailwind.config.ts
# Build passes
npm run build
```

---

### Scope Contract 2: Page Header Block
**Gap Coverage**: G-01 (Page Header — No overline, no anchor rule, no accent)

**Current State**: `ShopHeader.tsx` has centered layout, count under title, missing category path overline

**Target State**:
- Left-aligned layout
- Overline: "HEADPHONES · OPEN-BACK" in `accent.500` with `section-header-anchor` rule
- H1: `type-section-hed` with rule
- Result count moved to Controls Bar (see Contract 3)

**DoD — Pass 1: Skeleton**
- [ ] `ShopHeader.tsx`: semantic header > span + h1 structure
- [ ] Remove count span from component

**DoD — Pass 2: Data**
- [ ] Accept `categoryPath` prop (array of category names)
- [ ] Join with " · " separator
- [ ] Pass from `page.tsx` via metadata

**DoD — Pass 3: Build (Desktop → Mobile)**

*Layer 1 — Structure*
- [ ] Container: `header` > `div.flex.flex-col.gap-2`
- [ ] Overline wrapper: `span` + `::before` rule element
- [ ] Title: `h1`

*Layer 2 — Layout*
- [ ] Container: `flex flex-col gap-2 mb-8`
- [ ] Left-aligned (remove any centering)
- [ ] `section-header-anchor`: flex, gap-3, items-center

*Layer 3 — Surface*
- [ ] Overline: `.type-overline` + `text-accent-500` + `.section-header-anchor`
- [ ] Rule: 32px width, 1px height, `bg-brand-400`
- [ ] H1: `.type-section-hed`

*Layer 4 — Interaction*
- [ ] No hover states needed for header

**Verification**
```bash
npx playwright test --grep "ShopHeader"
npm run build
```

